    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup leans heavily into favorable matchups against mid-tier arms, headlined by **Corbin Carroll** (78.79) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.97). **Corbin Carroll** remains an essential start, as the park factors and his elite speed profile easily offset the slight penalty for facing a lefty in Kyle Freeland. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** is positioned for a breakout performance; his +14% platoon edge against Merrill Kelly, coupled with the pitcher's slow delivery\u2014offering a favorable environment for stolen base opportunities\u2014makes him one of our most efficient assets. **Josh Naylor** (73.25) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.71) also provide high-ceiling stability, with **Josh Naylor** capitalizing on the generous 4.93 xERA of Randy V\u00e1squez to maximize our RBI potential.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Cole Young**, whose 45.14 score was hampered almost exclusively by his projected #9 spot in the order. While his matchup against Randy V\u00e1squez suggested potential, the optimizer prioritized the higher-leverage spots of **James Wood** (68.08) and **Seiya Suzuki** (60.87), both of whom are projected in the top four of their respective lineups, ensuring more at-bat volume. We remain cautious regarding **Zach McKinstry** (45.92); his score sits near our floor, and any drop in his projected #6 spot could trigger a mid-day pivot if we look to bolster our average with more reliable bench depth.\n\nWe are operating under \"Lineup Pending\" status for the entire roster, which introduces inherent volatility. While we feel confident in the projections for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Dalton Rushing**, those Catcher slots are heavily reliant on them appearing in the middle-to-lower thirds of their lineups. We are also monitoring the risk associated with **Trevor Story** facing Spencer Strider; while the current score of 58.31 suggests a functional start, the SP skill of Strider remains a wildcard that could suppress our efficiency. We have opted to keep **Austin Riley** on the bench today, as he draws a tough matchup against an elite-leaning Connelly Early (2.92 xERA), confirming our commitment to prioritizing current-day matchup efficiency over historical reputation.",
